# Rosetta native corpus exclusions: files in native.index that one port does not run.
#
#   <port>[:<runner>]  <file>  <reason>
#
# port:   c python swift rust go zig java kotlin csharp csharp-bid
# runner: core wrapper net11 (net11: the csharp / csharp-bid Decimal128.Net11.Rosetta
#         program). Without a runner, the file is excluded from every runner of
#         that port.
# reason: required, the rest of the line. Remove the line when the reason no
#         longer holds.
#
# Example:
#   csharp:net11  transcendental_sweep.txt  runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48
#
# Checked by rosetta/check_native.py (run by CI).

# The D48 files (D48SwiftWorkOrder.md D-6, Phase 4, Phase 6): the transcendental
# sweeps and the pown/rootn oracle vectors.
# Every port runs them since its D48 switch (D-7). Only the net11 runners exclude
# them: they drive .NET 11's own Decimal128, not the port's D48.
csharp:net11     transcendental_sweep.txt          runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpWorkOrder.md CS-18)
csharp:net11     transcendental_stress.txt         runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpWorkOrder.md CS-18)
csharp:net11     transcendental_pown_rootn.txt     runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpWorkOrder.md CS-18)
csharp-bid:net11 transcendental_sweep.txt          runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpBidWorkOrder.md CB-7)
csharp-bid:net11 transcendental_stress.txt         runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpBidWorkOrder.md CB-7)
csharp-bid:net11 transcendental_pown_rootn.txt     runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpBidWorkOrder.md CB-7)

# transcendental_compound.txt (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md CX-6): compound lines a port
# that rounds 1 + x to 34 digits before the power gets wrong. Every port runs it
# since its compound commit; only the net11 runners exclude it.
csharp:net11     transcendental_compound.txt       runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's compound (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
csharp-bid:net11 transcendental_compound.txt       runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's compound (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)

# transcendental_large_n.txt (PownLargeNWorkOrder.md LN-7): pown / compound at |n| > 2^31. Ports
# whose n is 32-bit cannot take these arguments (LN-1); the 64-bit-n ports (swift,
# rust, zig, go) run it.
c                transcendental_large_n.txt        n is a 32-bit int: |n| > 2^31 is unreachable (PownLargeNWorkOrder.md LN-1)
python           transcendental_large_n.txt        n is a 32-bit int (the C engine's): |n| > 2^31 is unreachable (PownLargeNWorkOrder.md LN-1)
java             transcendental_large_n.txt        n is a 32-bit int: |n| > 2^31 is unreachable (PownLargeNWorkOrder.md LN-1)
kotlin           transcendental_large_n.txt        n is a 32-bit Int: |n| > 2^31 is unreachable (PownLargeNWorkOrder.md LN-1)
csharp           transcendental_large_n.txt        n is a 32-bit int: |n| > 2^31 is unreachable (PownLargeNWorkOrder.md LN-1)
csharp-bid       transcendental_large_n.txt        n is a 32-bit int: |n| > 2^31 is unreachable (PownLargeNWorkOrder.md LN-1)
